Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:03:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: v0.43 wire and checks, round 1 (src/types' last
 cycle gone; typedRules reads the kind table)

Commits 12 and 13's review (W-a-1, W-a-3). src/types/{party,roll,sending-stone,table} were still
one cycle group (amendment 1 (c), R1.4.9b). Its two closing edges go without moving a name:
FavoriteEntry's `target` is written out in src/types/sending-stone.ts and src/types/roll.ts's
FavoriteTarget reads it there (`NonNullable<FavoriteEntry['target']>`); EffectAsk is written
`{ type: 'save' | 'concentration' | 'check' }` instead of `Pick<TableAsk, 'type'>`. Every name
keeps its module, so no importer changes. A tsc probe holds FavoriteTarget, FavoriteInput,
FavoriteEntry['target'] and EffectAsk identical to before (and fails on a deliberate miss).

rollRequestSchema's typedRules asks the request-kind table whether a kind throws a d20
(`infoOf(kind).dice === 'd20'`) instead of reading EFFECT_DICE_KINDS: the same seven kinds
(roll-kinds.test.ts), so the same issues. The schema no longer imports that list; only the
values golden (C9) reads it now.

Types and one boolean only: no request, response, string or issue changes. L1 on this tree green (306 suites, 9,700 tests, 0 red;
tsc 0; eslint 0 errors, 659 warnings; gates 1-12 ok; gate 12: 2 cycle groups, base 4).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01821Sr9FKASxJn47SNudpbR
